  {
   "evidence": "`BaseChangeModule.toEnd_tmul_apply` (Subfield.lean:177-178) is proved by `simp [toEnd, mul_assoc]`, which works only because the reducible `abbrev` lets Mathlib's `Algebra.TensorProduct.map_tmul` (Maps.lean:542) fire. No lemma about `mapOpOpRight` exists (grep finds only its definition and the uses in Subfield.lean).",
   "file": "TauCeti/RingTheory/TensorProduct/Opposite.lean",
   "fix": "Add `@[simp] theorem mapOpOpRight_tmul (l : L) (a : A) : mapOpOpRight K L A (l \u2297\u209c a) = l \u2297\u209c op (op a) := (rfl)` and make the map a plain `def` without `@[expose]`.",
   "issue": "Public `Algebra.TensorProduct.mapOpOpRight` is an `abbrev` (reducible, definition exposed) with no `mapOpOpRight_tmul` lemma. Consumers can only evaluate it by unfolding the definition.",
   "line": 22
